# SQL View File Conventions

## Directives

SQL view files use comment-based directives:

```sql
-- @viewName: vw_active_products
-- @schema: public
-- @type: view
-- @dependsOn: vw_base_products, vw_categories
-- @indexes: idx_name(column1); idx_other(col2 DESC)
```

| Directive | Required | Description |
|-----------|----------|-------------|
| `@viewName` | No | Inferred from filename if omitted |
| `@schema` | No | Inferred from filename or defaults to `public` |
| `@type` | No | `view` (default) or `materialized` |
| `@dependsOn` | No | Comma-separated list of views this depends on |
| `@indexes` | No | Semicolon-separated index definitions (materialized only) |

## File Naming

Files are named: `[schema.]viewName.sql`

- `vw_active_products.sql` -> name: `vw_active_products`, schema: default
- `catalog.vw_products.sql` -> name: `vw_products`, schema: `catalog`

## Embedded Resources

SQL files must be embedded resources in the `.csproj`:

```xml
<ItemGroup>
  <EmbeddedResource Include="Views/**/*.sql" />
</ItemGroup>
```

## Materialized Views

- Set `@type: materialized`
- Use `@indexes` for CREATE INDEX statements
- Only PostgreSQL provider supports materialized views currently
- Refreshed at runtime via `context.RefreshMaterializedViewAsync()`
